{# enforcement/templates/status.md.tera — uses sahjhan v0.6.1 render context #}
# Holtz Status

**Project:** {{ protocol.name }} v{{ protocol.version }}
**State:** {{ state.label }}
**Ledger:** {{ ledger_len }} events
**Violations:** {{ violations }}
**Run:** {{ template_instance_id | default(value="?") }}
**Auditor:** holtz

## State Transitions
{% for e in events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="state_transition") -%}
- [x] {{ e.fields.from }} → **{{ e.fields.to }}** ({{ e.fields.command }})
{% endfor %}

## Perspectives ({{ sets.perspective.completed }}/{{ sets.perspective.total }})
{% for m in sets.perspective.members -%}
- [{% if m.done %}x{% else %} {% endif %}] {{ m.name }}
{% endfor %}

## Findings
{# Counted the way PUNCHLIST.md decides each row's Status: one bucket per
   finding id, resolved before deferred. Two views of one ledger must not be
   able to give different answers, and both previous expressions could.
   `unique_by` because a finding re-filed under an existing id is a correction,
   not a second finding — it renders as one punchlist row. Membership rather
   than `total - resolved - deferred` because those two sets are not disjoint:
   every deferral gates on `item_open` but `fix_commit` does not, so deferring
   a LOW and fixing it anyway drove Open to -1. #}
{% set findings = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") -%}
{% set resolved_ids = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding_resolved") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") | map(attribute="fields.id") -%}
{% set deferred_ids = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding_deferred") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") | map(attribute="fields.id") -%}
{% set_global open_count = 0 -%}
{% set_global resolved_count = 0 -%}
{% set_global deferred_count = 0 -%}
{% for f in findings -%}
{% if resolved_ids is containing(f.fields.id) %}{% set_global resolved_count = resolved_count + 1 %}
{%- elif deferred_ids is containing(f.fields.id) %}{% set_global deferred_count = deferred_count + 1 %}
{%- else %}{% set_global open_count = open_count + 1 %}{% endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
**Open:** {{ open_count }} | **Resolved:** {{ resolved_count }} | **Deferred:** {{ deferred_count }} | **Total:** {{ findings | length }}
